{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789899518,"nonce":"bbf/+stvd1VTxFb4hQc7/+qc2sE=","title":"Lua: no C stack, so calls from the library into the program nest without limit","message":"The reference bounds calls made from C into Lua (pcall, xpcall, metamethods, iterators, comparators, resume) at LUAI_MAXCCALLS, raising 'C stack overflow'; here they nested up to the depth limit, so a recursion through pcall ran 200000 deep instead of 200 (calls.lua 'C-stack overflow while handling C-stack overflow', cstack.lua). Alongside: a message handler that raised propagated its error instead of being called again on it and ending in 'error in error handling'; assert did not position a string message as error does; coroutine.wrap did not put its caller's position in front of a string error; a __call handler that was itself a table with __call was refused.","files":null}]}